Let's say you have a table with `orderId` and `productId` forming the composite primary key.

```java
package com.example.model;

import javax.persistence.*;

@Entity
@IdClass(OrderIdProductId.class)
public class OrderItem {

    @Id
    private Long orderId;

    @Id
    private Long productId;

    // Other fields...

    // Getters and setters for orderId and productId
}

public class OrderIdProductId implements java.io.Serializable {
    private Long orderId;
    private Long productId;

    public OrderIdProductId(Long orderId, Long productId) {
        this.orderId = orderId;
        this.productId = productId;
    }

    // Getters and setters
    public Long getOrderId() {
        return orderId;
    }

    public void setOrderId(Long orderId) {
        this.orderId = orderId;
    }

    public Long getProductId() {
        return productId;
    }

    public void setProductId(Long productId) {
        this.productId = productId;
    }
}
```

