    // getters and setters...
}
```

In this case, the `PromotionBenefit` entity has an embedded primary key represented by the `PromotionBenefitPK` class.

Note that in both cases, you need to define a separate class (e.g. `PromotionBenefitPK`) that represents the composite primary key and implements the `Serializable` interface.

As for using multiple columns as a primary key with JPA CriteriaBuilder, you can use the `in()` method on a `Path` object to create an IN predicate with multiple values.

