        }
      },
      {
        '$person.lastName$': {
          $ilike: `%s%`
        }
      }
    ]
  })
  .getOne()
```

This will generate the following SQL query:

```sql
SELECT attendance.childId, child.class, CONCAT(child.firstName, child.lastName) 
FROM attendance 
INNER JOIN child ON attendance.child = child 
WHERE (attendance.userName ILIKE '%s%' OR child.firstName ILIKE '%s%' OR child.lastName ILIKE '%s%')
```

Note that the `$or` operator is used inside the `where` object to specify multiple conditions. Each condition is an object with a key-value pair, where the key is the field name and the value is the condition.

Also, note that the `%s%` is used for the ILIKE operator, which is equivalent to the LIKE operator in SQL. The `%` character matches any sequence of characters before or after the specified string.

